==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*5 [[Devil Wife|Devil Wives]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 43.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Wicked Face]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Malevolent Dark Cat]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is filled to the brim with a wide variety of hard-pushing [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] threats, consisting of one dangerous midranger, a backliner, and many, many melee units.

The boss, Malevolent Dark Cat, is bulky and comes with a [[Shield]] that effectively doubles his health, so any [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]] like [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] are highly recommended. The peons in this stage are not too threatening if you're decently prepared, so stalling them won't be too hard if you have specialist meatshields like [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]]. Do note that without units that can curse Malevolent Dark like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]], [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] won't be of any help here as Malevolent Dark will curse it, turning it into a massive cash drain. Speaking of Uril, owning his [[True Form]] makes this stage trivial, albeit creating a lot of [[Surge Attack|Surges]] from Malevolent Dark Cat's Counter-Surge ability, meaning [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune units]] are recommended.

Money in this stage won't be an issue, as the Devil Wives spawn consistently enough to provide you with a constant cash flow. However, you can try to use [[:Category:Cats with Money Up ability|cats with Money Up abilities]] like a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] to snipe the Devil Wives for a huge sum of cash at a time.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] - An excellent meatshield in this stage, Cone Cat's resistance against Aku works very well as every enemy in the stage is within its target traits. Its Curse Immunity dismisses Malevolent Dark Cat's primary ability, allowing it to continue holding the front as your remaining units rain fire from behind. Maize Cat works best with Research [[Cat Combo|Combos]], putting its very high durability to great use. Its only notable weakness is its lack of Surge Immunity.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] - Boulder's extreme health as well as Slow/Surge/[[Wave Attack|Wave]] Immunity ensures nothing gets past during its brief lifetime. It is often useful as a defensive support option, and is best combined with research combos to increase its uptime in case if your other meatshields fail.
*[[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]]/[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] - Go-to specialists for removing shields known for their reliability, they can be used to significantly reduce Malevolent Dark Cat's durability and render it vulnerable to crowd-control effects, especially considering its tough Shield fully regenerates each time it gets knocked back. However, both have their drawbacks. Cat Researcher is very fragile, can be destroyed by Surges, and his Single Attack means peons can stop him from hitting Malevolent Dark Cat. Barrel, being reliant on its LD, can't outrange Malevolent Dark Cat, so a small shift in the frontline will likely result in Malevolent Dark Cat destroying it immediately.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] - Esoteric Uril is a great choice for strategies without [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]], having both Slow and Curse against Aku. With Slow, he can stop the advancement of Malevolent Dark and the other Aku peons, and Curse lets you be able to use Cactus if you don't have Cone. Uril also has Curse and Surge immunity to top him off. But, even with all this said, Uril still has some small drawbacks. The first issue is his obtainability, since climbing up the [[Infernal Tower]] is pretty hard for some players, but this is only a small issue since by the time you play [[:Category:Malevolent Stages|Malevolent Stages]], you have probably completed [[Uncanny Legends]] at this point and have the Uncanny Legends [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]]' True Forms to tear apart [[Infernal Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]] of the Infernal Tower. Another small issue is that Uril doesn't have Shield Piercing, meaning you will have to bring a dedicated Shield Piercer to break Malevolent Dark's shield for Uril to apply his crowd-control effects to it.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mohawk Cat]] - Having his True Form will make this stage a lot easier, as being immune to curse allows it to dodge attacks from Malevolent Dark as well as the other Aku enemies.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]] - A powerful Long Distance crowd-control unit with Surge Immunity, Satoru has 50% chance to pierce Shields, and should his hit connect, it'll delay the threats by causing knockback and slowing them for 6 seconds, which can be all the difference you make as he helps recovering ground.
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]] - A backline [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attacker]] built for damage, her curse ability can completely shut down Malevolent Dark Cat's main gimmick once its Shield comes down, allowing Cat Cactus free reign. Her Surges are indeed duped by Malevolent Dark Cat without the Shield, and while she is immune to them, using her requires a dedicated formation that can fully dismiss these Counter-Surges.
*[[Lucifer the Fallen (Uber Rare Cat)|Lucifer]] - With his strong ability against Aku, Surge Immunity and the ability to generate an equally powerful level 1 Surge, Lucifer's LD attacks can put a serious dent to anything he hits at a great range. While Surge duplication generally isn't an issue, he does have a very large blind spot that one must account for.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama]] - The Aku-nuking brawler is a great pick for this stage due to his offense and defense against Akus, guaranteed Sheild Pierce, and Curse Immune against Malevolent Dark Cat. If any supporting Aku enemies happen to creep past your frontline and get within Hanayama's range, they aren't surviving his attack. That being said, don't fully rely on him, as he'll likely last until Malevolent Dark Cat is near the point of Strengthening, so bring supporting hard-hitters with him, such as the other recommended units listed.

